			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:13</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>MOSTRA_VALOR_CAMP_DBF (13)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Shows the contents of a field for a given set of records, indexed from 1.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Showing the contents of a field for a set of records, indexed from 1.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>13</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NomCamp</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Field Name</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of the field of the DBF table.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FieldName"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>RegIni</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Initial Record</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Record index starting from 1 where it starts working or '*' starting from the end of the table.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:IniRec"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>RegFi</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Final Record</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Record index starting from 1 where it stops working or '*' in order to continue until the end of the table.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FiRec"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:14</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>JOIN_TAULES_DBF (14)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Allows the joining in a single table of fields belonging to two different DBF tables. It is necessary to establish a correspondence between both tables through one or several links between equivalent fields of the two tables; these fields are named key fields. In most cases there is enough with defining a single key field on each table (as it is stated in Example 1) in order to define clearly the correspondence between the records of both tables. In some cases, nevertheless, it is needed to define more than one key field in one or in both implied tables (Example 2) in order to define clearly the correspondence between both tables: the combination of these fields is called combined key. It is also needed to define all the fields which are shown in the output table, the result of join. If it is wanted that key fields appear in the output table too, they must be included in the desired field list because it may be desired that they only act as links, but not figuring in the resulting table of the join operation.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[Generating a new resulting table (DBFFileResulting) from a join between the DBFFileMain and DBFFileSecondary tables with one or multiple links. The links are indicated from the key fields /T1_CLAU# (for table 1) and /T2_CLAU# (for table 2) and the fields present in the resulting table are indicated from their origins with /T1_CAMP# (for table 1) and /T2_CAMP# (for table 2). # is the field number, indexed from 1 <b><u>for each table</u></b>.]]></ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>14</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBFPrincipal</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Main DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Main DBF file of the fusion on tables in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:MainDBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBFSecundari</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Secondary DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Secondary DBF file of the fusion on tables in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:SecondaryDBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>T1_CLAU#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>T1_CLAU#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Names of the key fields of the main table T1, with which the connection between the two tables is established in order to carry out the join. # indicates the order of the key fields linked, indexed from 1. If more than one field is stated, it is understood that it is desired to perform as a combined key.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>T2_CLAU#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>T2_CLAU#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Names of the the key fields of the associated table T2, with which the connection between the two tables is established in order to carry out the join. # indicates the order of key fields linked, indexed from 1. If more than one field is stated, it is understood that it is desired to perform as a combined key.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>T1_CAMP#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>T1_CAMP#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Names of the fields of the T1 table that will make up the resulting table. # indicates the order (correlative  and beginning by 1).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>T2_CAMP#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>T2_CAMP#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Names of the fields of the T2 table that will make up the resulting table. # indicates the order (correlative  and beginning by 1).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>RELACIO_1_N</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>1 to N relation</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Indicates that a multiple cardinality relationship is possible between a record of the main table and n records of the associated table. Its absence does not permit this multiple relationship.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NOMES_REG_ENLLAC</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Only  Records Link</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This parameter implies that only are stored in the result table those records contained in the main table that have correspondence in the associated  table.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBFResultat</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF Result File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>DBF result file in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFResultFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:15</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>ORDENA_TAULA_DBF (15)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Carries out an ordering process for one or multiple criteria of a DBF table. The ordered table is generated in a new DBF file and it is possible to establish an ascending or descending order for each criterion.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Generates a new resulting table (DBFFileResulting) from an ordering defined by one or n criteria indicated by /CAMP_#. For each field or criterion it is possible to define an ascending (default) or descending order using /ORDRE_#.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>15</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBFOrigen</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Origin DBF file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>DBF origin file in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:OriginDBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>CAMP_#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>CAMP_#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Names of the fields that will be part of the resulting table. # is an order number (correlative and starting from 1).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>ORDRE_#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>ORDRE_#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>"D" or "d "indicates a descending order and "A" or "a" an ascending order (default).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBFResultat</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF Result File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>DBF result file in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFResultFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:16</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>SUPR_REGISTRE_DBF (16)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Eliminates one or more consecutive records of a DBF table. If it is wanted to specify a range, RegFi must be stated as well. RegFi record will be also erased.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Eliminates one or more consecutive records of a DBF table. If you wish to specify an interval, you should also indicate FiRec. The FiRec record will also be erased.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>16</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>RegIni</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Initial Record</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Record index starting from 1 where it starts working or '*' starting from the end of the table.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:IniRec"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>RegFi</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Final Record</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Record index starting from 1 where it stops working or '*' in order to continue until the end of the table.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FiRec"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:17</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>JOIN_TOTS_ENLLACOS (17)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Makes as many joins as physical links is the main table and its associated tables, only to get a flat table (DBF format) with all fields of all tables associated, except the key fields of child tables that involve unnecessary repetition . The relationship indicated in the metadata rule style join (or RELACIO_1_N RELACIO_N_1). To perform this task, convert the ODBC tables to DBF, which can generate truncated  in field names and changes of types and sizes. In addition, the maximum field name of the supertable is limited to 256 (limit of the resulting DBF).</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Generates the 'flat table' (not relational) DBFResultFile, from the physical joins between the main table and associated tables indicated in the corresponding DBFMainTable REL file.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>17</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBFTaulaPrincipal</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF Main Table</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Main table file in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFMainTable"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBFResultat</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF Result File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>DBF result file in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFResultFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:18</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>MULTIREGISTRE_A_MULTICAMP (18)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Transforms multirecord into multifield. To define multirecord, repetitions of key field values is taken as a criterion (typically graphic identifier field). The fields are replicated as many fields as often as the maximum number of repetitions of the key field values.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Transforms multirecord into multifield. To define multirecord, repetitions of key field values is taken as a criterion (typically graphic identifier field). The fields between FieldName FieldNameUntil are replicated to multiple fields with a similar name (with an incremental index added) as many times as the maximum number of repetitions of values FieldKeyName (they are added after the field FieldNameAfter; typically FieldNameAfter and FieldNameUntil are the same).</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>18</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NomCampClau</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Field Key Name</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of  the field of the DBF table that acts as a key field.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FieldKeyName"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NomCamp</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Field Name</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of the field of the DBF table.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FieldName"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NomCampFinsA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Field Name Until</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Field name that closes the interval, or '*' if you wish to continue until the last field.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FieldNameUntil"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NomCampDespresDe</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Field Name After</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of the field after which the selected operation is carried out (create, erase, etc), or '*' if it must be done before the first or ']' if it must be done after the last.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param6"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FieldNameAfter"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
