	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:20</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>PAS_DE_ODBC_A_ODBC (20)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Allows the generation of a database table from another table, view or selection (from a SQL statement) of another database. Access to the database is via ODBC driver and therefore databases can be different from each other and from any type (MS Access, Oracle, SQL Server ...). The application will create a duplicate table, or view selection, following as closely as possible to the original format of the table when data types, sizes, restrictions ... (there are specific types of data each manager and there are no others, these chosen type with similar characteristics). This option is useful when we have systems database servers and types of information we need to send someone external not have access to the database, for example if we have a database type of Oracle or SQL Server. In this case, the information can be exported into a database such as MS Access, in order to have all data in a single file.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Allows the generation of a database table from another table, view or selection (from a SQL statement) of another database.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>20</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerBDOrigen</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DB Origin File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Origin database. DSN file or a file-type database (as it is an MDB) accessible through ODBC.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBOriginFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/octet-stream</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/octet-stream</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-msaccess</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binay</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TaulaOrigen</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Origin Table to convert</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>It may be a table, view or an SQL query about the ODBC database (if the sentence requires inverted commas, a diaresis must be used instead).</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:OriginTable"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TaulaResultat</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Result Table</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Table result of the conversion.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:ResultTable"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerBDResultat</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>BD Result File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Result database. DSN file or a file-type database (as it is an MDB) accessible through ODBC.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:BDResultFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/octet-stream</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/octet-stream</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-msaccess</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binay</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:21</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>PURGA_TAULA_DBF (21)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Determines if there are records that have been marked as deleted but is still on the table. In this case, they are physically removed. The date of the file is only changed when records to be deleted are found. Most MiraMon programs ignore the erase mark and consider the records marked as deleted as normal records from the table. Whether it both Excel and Access does not show the records marked as deleted DBF's ODBC driver uses to execute a SQL statement DELETE.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Records that have been marked as deleted are physically removed from the file.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>21</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:22</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>OMPLE_CAMP_TANTP_CENT_A_DBF (22)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Fills a field with the percentage values obtained from  the ratio of a field that contains a partial value and the total value.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Fills a field with the percentage values obtained from the ratio of a field that contains a partial value and the total value.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>22</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NomCampTantPCent</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>File Name %</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Field to be filled with the values obtained from the ratio of FileNamePartial and FileNameTotal.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FileNamePcent"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NomCampParcial</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>File Name partial</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File Name Partial</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FileNamePartial"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NomCampTotal</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>File Name Total</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File Name Total</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FileNameTotal"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SUMA_CENT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Up to 100</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Calculated percentages add up to 100.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:23</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>COMPLETA_JOIN_1_A_N (23)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Completes the table with the values that can be missing in reviewing a JOIN 1 to N between the table and a thesaurus from the key fields that make the link and the fields to complete. Once the JOIN is established between the two tables, it is checked whether the values of the fields to be completed that come from the thesaurus are present in the table and otherwise, they are incorporated as more records for that graphic identifier.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Completed the result table (FileDBF) with the values that may be missing in reviewing a 1 to N join between the DBFFile and the DBFfileSecondary from one or multiple links.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>23</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBFSecundari</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Secondary DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Secondary DBF file of the fusion on tables in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:SecondaryDBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>T1_CLAU#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>T1_CLAU#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Names of the key fields of the main table T1, with which the connection between the two tables is established in order to carry out the join. # indicates the order of the key fields linked, indexed from 1. If more than one field is stated, it is understood that it is desired to perform as a combined key.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>T2_CLAU#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>T2_CLAU#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Names of the the key fields of the associated table T2, with which the connection between the two tables is established in order to carry out the join. # indicates the order of key fields linked, indexed from 1. If more than one field is stated, it is understood that it is desired to perform as a combined key.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>T1_CAMP#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>T1_CAMP#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Names of the fields of the T1 table that will make up the resulting table. # indicates the order (correlative  and beginning by 1).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>T2_CAMP#</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>T2_CAMP#</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Names of the fields of the T2 table that will make up the resulting table. # indicates the order (correlative  and beginning by 1).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GestBD:param1:24</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>ELEMENT_XML_A_DBF (24)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[Writes in a cell of a DBF the XML node pointed by the xpath as a text. It is intended to retrieve the value of the "leaf" nodes of the document elements tree whether elements or attributes. In a document such as: <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>                <MD_Metadata>                    <fileIdentifier>5400031_full28_ca</fileIdentifier>                                    <hierarchyLevel>                                      <MD_ScopeCode value="series" />                                    </hierarchyLevel>                </MD_Metadata>  to request the xpath "MD_Metadata/fileIdentifier" recovers:  "5400031_full28_ca" to request the xpath "MD_Metadata/hierarchyLevel/MD_ScopeCode/@value" recovers:  "series".<br>  Remember that if the xpath of a node that is not "leaf" is requested, the values of all the child elements separated by spaces will be obtained,  result that does not seem too useful.<br/>  Be careful with xpath like this:  /bookstore/book[1]/title  "IE5 and later has implemented that [0] should be the first node, but according to the W3C standard it should have been [1]. </br>  In MiraMon, using Windows libraries (which are from IE5) is this "characteristic", that is to say, that the arrays of nodes begin to be numbered from 0 and not from 1.]]></ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Fills a cell in a DBF with the values (if QueExtr='V') or the names (if QueExtr='N') of an element or attribute designated by an XPath of an XML document. If the XPath results in more than one item, it fills more than one consecutive record for that field. In case (if QueExtr='C') it fills the cell with the number of nodes that meet the xpath.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>24</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerXML</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>XML File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>XML File</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:XMLFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/xml</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/xml</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>RegIni</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Initial Record</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Record index starting from 1 where it starts working or '*' starting from the end of the table.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:IniRec"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>NomCamp</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Field Name</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of the field of the DBF table.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:FieldName"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>XPath</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>XPath</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Xpath of the XML document referring to the part of the document to extract the information.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param6"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:XPath"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>QueExtr</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>What to extract</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>If QueExtr='V' fills the cell with the value of the element or the attribute designated by a XPath, if QueExtr='N' fills the cell with the name of the element or the designated attribute for a XPath and if QueExtr='C' fills the cell with the number of nodes that meet the xpath.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param7"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:WhatExtract"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>V</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>N</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>C</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDBF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DBF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File in classical DBF format (dBASE III, dBASE III+ or dBASE IV) or extended DBF of MiraMon.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DBFFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
